'OK
' AND and OR stop as soon as the answer is known. The right operand here would fail at run
' time if it were ever evaluated, so reaching the end is the proof.
PROGRAM P
    DECLARE z INTEGER
    z = 0
    ASSERT "AND does not evaluate its right operand after FALSE", NOT (FALSE AND 10 / z = 1)
    ASSERT "OR does not evaluate its right operand after TRUE", TRUE OR 10 / z = 1
END.
